.TH QORE-EXTRACT-QM-METADATA 1 "2026 May 14" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qore-extract-qm-metadata \- extract structured API metadata from a Qore source file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qore-extract-qm-metadata
\fIsource-file\fP
[\fIoutput-file\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqore-extract-qm-metadata\fR uses the \fBQoreApiMetadata\fR module to parse a
Qore source file (\fB.qm\fP, \fB.qc\fP or \fB.q\fP) and emit a JSON document
describing its public API: classes, methods, functions, constants, hashdecls,
enums and namespaces.
.PP
The tool is invoked at build time by the Qore CMake rules to populate
\fI/usr/share/qore/metadata/\fP, which is consumed by tools such as
\fBqls\fP(1) (the Qore Language Server) and the Qore documentation index.
.PP
If \fIoutput-file\fP is omitted the JSON document is written to standard output.
.PP
If the \fBjson\fR binary module is not available (missing or ABI-incompatible
with the running \fBqore\fR), the tool emits a warning on standard error and
writes an empty JSON object so that the build can continue.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I source-file
Required.
Path to a Qore source file (\fB.qm\fP, \fB.qc\fP or \fB.q\fP).
.TP
.I output-file
Optional.
If given, JSON is written to this file (truncating any prior contents);
otherwise it is written to standard output.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success (including the json-unavailable graceful path).
.TP
.B 1
Missing or unreadable source file.
